{"reference":"Luke 24","book":"Luke","chapter":24,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"language_literary","title":"The Emmaus Story","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The Emmaus account is shaped as a movement from failed recognition to understanding and witness. The travelers do not recognize Jesus at first; Scripture is interpreted along the road, hospitality is offered at the meal, and they recognize him in the breaking of bread before returning at once to report what happened. Cleopas is named, but his companion is not, so the passage does not identify that second traveler.","verse_refs":["Luke 24:13-35"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_luke_024_c8d82a37dd2c865c3b7a9ecd"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"}]},{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"The Risen Jesus and Luke’s Ending","blocks":[{"id":"block_2","text":"In Luke 24:36-49, Jesus invites the disciples to touch him and eats fish before them in response to their fear that they are seeing a spirit. The passage therefore presents these actions as an answer to that fear. Historical, metaphysical, and doctrinal conclusions drawn from this scene should be distinguished from the narrative’s own claims. The ending also has textual variation concerning the wording about being carried into heaven and the disciples’ worship; Acts 1 narrates an ascension after a further period of appearances, so the two accounts should be compared rather than silently harmonized.","verse_refs":["Luke 24:36-49","Luke 24:50-53"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_luke_024_ffbabe0003a9d01ba0affb67"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed"},{"id":"block_3","text":"Acts describes Jesus’ ascent with a cloud and angelic interpretation. This imagery draws on biblical theophanic imagery—imagery associated with divine appearance—rather than providing a modern physical mechanism for the event. That distinction helps frame how the closing scene of Luke is being narrated.","verse_refs":["Luke 24:50-53"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_luke_024_995fe04209bc7841522ce704"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}